Reinstate win_third_party_warn_as_error.

Chromium 37 had a win_third_party_warn_as_error variable controlling
warnings-as-errors for third-party code. Chromium 49 dropped it and hardcoded
'WarnAsError': 'true' instead.

That setting lives in a target_conditions block, and target_conditions are
evaluated per target *after* target_defaults has been merged in -- so they
overwrite anything a project sets there. The result is that a project embedding
Chromium's build cannot turn third-party warnings-as-errors off at all, and any
warning MSVC has added since 2016 becomes a hard error in code the project does
not own. ICU is the case in point:

  error C2220: the following warning is treated as an error
  third_party/icu/source/common/uresbund.c(969)

This restores the variable, keeping upstream's 'true' as the default so
behaviour is unchanged unless a project overrides it. Sawbuck sets it to
'false' in sawbuck/sawbuck.gypi while the VS2022 port is in progress; the
first-party equivalent is sawbuck_warn_as_error, next to it.

--- a/build/common.gypi
+++ b/build/common.gypi
@@ -1184,6 +1184,11 @@
     'component%': '<(component)',
     'win_analyze%': '<(win_analyze)',
     'win_fastlink%': '<(win_fastlink)',
+
+    # PATCHED: reinstated. Chromium 37 had this variable and Chromium 49
+    # dropped it, hardcoding WarnAsError for third-party code instead. See the
+    # use site below.
+    'win_third_party_warn_as_error%': 'true',
     'enable_resource_whitelist_generation%': '<(enable_resource_whitelist_generation)',
     'use_titlecase_in_grd%': '<(use_titlecase_in_grd)',
     'remoting%': '<(remoting)',
@@ -3153,7 +3158,11 @@
             'msvs_settings': {
               'VCCLCompilerTool': {
                 'WarningLevel': '3',
-                'WarnAsError': 'true',
+                # PATCHED: was hardcoded 'true'. This block sits in
+                # target_conditions, which are evaluated per target *after*
+                # target_defaults is merged, so it overwrites anything set
+                # there -- a project cannot turn it off without this variable.
+                'WarnAsError': '<(win_third_party_warn_as_error)',
                 'Detect64BitPortabilityProblems': 'false',
               },
             },
